<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lützen (1632)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Lützen · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lützen was fought in 1632 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War between the Swedish army and imperial forces under Wallenstein. The Swedes held the field, but King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> was killed during the fighting. The battle is a landmark in the military history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>, whose reformed army under Gustavus had transformed European warfare.</p></div>
